{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":751106,"ns":0,"title":"Anchoring effect","extract":"The anchoring effect is a psychological phenomenon in which an individual's judgments or decisions are influenced by a reference point or \"anchor\" which can be completely irrelevant.\nThe original description of the anchoring effect came from psychophysics.","description":"Tendency to base judgments on an irrelevant anchor","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}